WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.472
In the late stage of the Chu–Han contention, Xiang Yu's army was surrounded layer upon layer by the Han army at Gaixia.

00:00:05.822 --> 00:00:10.094
Night fell, and the campfires in the camp went out one by one.

00:00:10.444 --> 00:00:15.916
Deep in the night, songs of Chu drifted in from all sides — melodious and sorrowful.

00:00:16.266 --> 00:00:20.298
The singing drifted in from every direction, like the wind — everywhere at once.

00:00:20.648 --> 00:00:24.608
The soldiers listened intently, unable to tell dream from reality.

00:00:24.958 --> 00:00:29.878
Hearing the songs, the Chu soldiers' hearts broke — they believed their homeland had already been taken by the Han army.

00:00:30.228 --> 00:00:33.660
They thought of their families far away, and their tears could not help falling.

00:00:34.010 --> 00:00:38.810
With morale shattered, Xiang Yu led his remaining troops in a breakout — but in the end, he failed.

00:00:39.160 --> 00:00:43.528
After dawn, only silence and sorrow remained on the battlefield.

00:00:43.878 --> 00:00:48.030
Xiang Yu gazed into the distance, his heart full of helplessness and sorrow.

00:00:48.380 --> 00:00:54.908
The idiom 'Songs of Chu from All Sides' has been handed down, describing a person beset on every side, isolated and without help.

00:00:55.258 --> 00:00:58.690
When we meet a desperate situation, we need calm and courage all the more.

